2. meta-rules-dat (GeoIP / GeoSite data)
----------------------------------------

Project: MetaCubeX/meta-rules-dat
URL:     https://github.com/MetaCubeX/meta-rules-dat
License: GNU General Public License, version 3
Files:   Country.mmdb (country-lite.mmdb) and geosite.dat, downloaded at
         build time and included in builds.

The databases are generated by the upstream project from several public
sources. See the upstream repository and its README for the full list of
sources and their licenses, including (but not limited to):

  - Loyalsoldier/geoip
  - v2fly/domain-list-community (MIT)
  - Loyalsoldier/domain-list-custom
  - felixonmars/dnsmasq-china-list
  - gfwlist/gfwlist
  - cokebar/gfwlist2dnsmasq
  - Loyalsoldier/cn-blocked-domain
  - AdblockPlus/EasylistChina + Easylist
  - AdGuard DNS filter
  - Peter Lowe's ad server list
  - Dan Pollock's hosts file
  - crazy-max/WindowsSpyBlocker
  - blackmatrix7/ios_rule_script

Because these data files are distributed by the upstream project under
GPL-3.0, redistribution of builds that include them is subject to GPL-3.0.
The complete corresponding source of ClashBrowser is this repository; the
data itself can be obtained from the upstream project.


3. MaxMind GeoLite2 data
------------------------

The `Country.mmdb` database is derived from MaxMind GeoLite2 data
(GeoLite2-Country), as processed by MetaCubeX/meta-rules-dat.

This product includes GeoLite2 data created by MaxMind, available from
https://www.maxmind.com.

Use and redistribution of GeoLite2 data are governed by MaxMind's terms
(GeoLite2 End User License Agreement and, where applicable, CC BY-SA 4.0).
Users and redistributors of builds containing this data are responsible for
complying with those terms, including attribution and the requirement to keep
GeoLite data reasonably up to date.


